  "$comment": "Asset registry. Every game media file has exactly one entry here and one row in ASSETS.md. Raw sources live in art/raw/<id>.png (user-provided); `pnpm assets` writes normalized output + public/game/assets.json (generated, never committed). All sizes are final art pixels. Strips: `baseline` = y of the line the art stands on (lowest opaque row = baseline - 1); `ruler: true` = when the source is green-screen, its leftmost frame is a size reference that is dropped (transparent sources never carry one). `backgroundThreshold` overrides the black flood-fill threshold for a raw file. Sets: items in reading order (rows top→bottom, left→right), each fitted into its `size` (or, with `fill`, scaled to its exact width and aligned top/bottom); item `anchors` are relative to the item box. `anchors` = [x, y, w, h] rects (w = h = 0 for a point) where the game draws on the art; values here are the placeholder geometry, the pipeline re-detects them on delivered art.",
